      "body": "COMPLETE REPRESENTABILITY (Wave 4 / divRep) - START HERE `agent-ready`\n\nGOAL: land `divRep` (Div^g-lite representable), then the datum tail, concluding `AJCR.w4-rep` (Pic^0 representability). Orient from roadmap node `AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr` and the earlier inbox trail `I-0289...I-0307`.\n\nAUDITED STATE (2026-07-20): the previous claim that only a bounded total-stalk bridge remained is false. The chart reading map has an `R`-linear range `P`; RD-N concerns the genuine chart ideal `J = B * P`, where `B = Gamma(V)`. The landed flatness is flatness of `B/P` as an `R`-module, not purity or flatness of `B/J` after quotienting by a chosen section.\n\nGuard example: `R = k[epsilon]/(epsilon^2)`, `B = R[t]`, `P = R*t + R*(t^2+epsilon)`, `s=t`. The reduced fibre is generated by `t` and `B/P` is `R`-free, but `J/(s)=(epsilon)` has nonzero fibre at `(epsilon,t)`. Thus an achiever and a total-stalk lift alone cannot prove RD-N.\n\nCORRECT CRITICAL PATH: use the second Grassmannian window to prove relative multiplication persistence `K_prime = H_s * K` from P-fib in every residue field, globalize fibre-surjectivity by finite-module Nakayama, then prove the resulting ideal-level purity/local principality. Only then derive `SeedUnivRDN` and unconditional `isGenerator` -> certificate/U1 -> F5/F6/F7 -> `divRep`.\n\nVALID LANDED INFRASTRUCTURE: residue-point lift `abac842cc` (`DivSchemeFibrePoint.lean`); sharp single-point `kappa(z)` consumer `ca7c437d4`; genuine `chartReadIdeal` and equality with the old colength module `e0a718b0c`; finite fibre-surjectivity/Nakayama globalization `b67d9b09`, `77e1f3bd`. The draft Quot/FGA project is typed-sorry dependent and is not a complete shortcut.\n\nBINDING: stay single-point for the RD-N consumer, but do not mistake single-point fibre divisibility for ideal purity; do not reuse the old chart-flat inference or the dead global `kappa(p)` bridge.",
